# Thesis repository — agent rules

**Before any thesis, plan, benchmark, or artefact edit: read `AGENT.md` in the repo root.**

## Document roles (do not confuse these)

| Document | Status |
| --- | --- |
| `Thesis_Plan_v2.tex` / `.pdf` | **Supervisor-facing, reviewed** |
| `Thesis_v1.tex` / `.pdf` | **Supervisor-facing, reviewed** (skeleton; ch. 6–9 empty unless author asks) |
| `Thesis_POC.tex` / `.pdf` | **Full draft** — canonical but still needs review |
| `spec/`, `cpp/`, `rust/`, `bench/`, `faults/`, `ffi/` | Evidence — must match thesis claims |

When claims, RQs, methodology, or numbers change: sync plan + v1 + `Thesis_POC.tex`; regenerate via `bench/refresh_thesis.sh` (never hand-edit `figures/gen_macros.tex`).

## Grade criteria (Finnish 1–5) — every edit must protect these

| # | Criterion | Grade | Blocker to 5 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Objectives & RQs | 5 | Keep falsifiable RQ2 (5 in-guarantee + 2 boundary defects) |
| 2 | Scholarly sources | 5 | Acknowledge contrary results; consistent terminology |
| 3 | Method & data | 4.5 | Bare-metal tail campaign; counters for RSS/op gap |
| 4 | Results presentation | 4.5 | RQ1 far tail open on the virtualised host; figures must match tables |
| 5 | Discussion | 5 | No over-claim: “cannot tell” ≠ “equivalent” |
| 6 | Academic text | 5 | No figure–text contradictions; check abstract page overflow |

Full notes: `ASSESSMENT.md`. Checklist per edit: `AGENT.md` §2.

## Non-negotiable claims

- Frozen spec + parity suite; interleaved design + Holm-corrected paired tests.
- The measurement host is a virtualised KVM guest: the **far tail below saturation** is unresolved there. The overload divergence and the resource results are resolved.
- Peak RSS: real language + allocator effect; allocator effect is larger.
- End-to-end sweep ≈ handoff cost; the operation is a fraction of a percent of it — do not bound a language effect from that sweep.
- Rust: data races/aliasing at compile time; **not** race conditions or deadlocks.
- Quote numbers via `figures/gen_macros.tex` macros; never transcribe them into prose, slides, or scripts.

## After substantive changes

Run `bench/refresh_thesis.sh` when numbers change (it regenerates figures/tables, the colloquium deck, and `Thesis_POC.pdf`); rebuild `Thesis_v1.tex` / `Thesis_Plan_v2.tex` when their sources change. Zero LaTeX errors and undefined refs required.

## Do not

- Treat `Thesis_POC.pdf` as supervisor-approved.
- Fill `Thesis_v1.tex` chapters 6–9 without explicit author request.
- Commit unless explicitly asked.
